I'd live to do it.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.163
I'd do it even without getting paid.

00:10:11.163 --> 00:10:12.873
So that's when I created
a 10 year plan in there

00:10:12.873 --> 00:10:14.844
and just came out and
started executing on it.

00:10:14.844 --> 00:10:17.638
Don't just do a record
because it's the hot record

00:10:17.638 --> 00:10:19.967
right now and you trying to
make one that sounds like it,

00:10:19.967 --> 00:10:23.220
assuming it's going to give you
a better shot 'cause it's not.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.982
That record is already
there, so your record

00:10:25.982 --> 00:10:27.452
is not going to make a difference.

00:10:27.452 --> 00:10:30.296
So do not try to copy what
you're hearing out there.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:32.973
- How can record companies
become profitable again?

00:10:32.973 --> 00:10:35.157
I noticed last year they eked out

00:10:35.157 --> 00:10:37.924
a small, very small profit.

00:10:37.924 --> 00:10:39.597
I think like 0.2%.

00:10:39.597 --> 00:10:41.403
- And I think it's going to get smaller.

00:10:41.403 --> 00:10:44.470
I think unfortunately,
as the record companies,

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.620
they're not thinking outside the box.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.617
They're using old methods
of how they used to

00:10:48.617 --> 00:10:50.583
market, promote and they
don't know how to let that go.

00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:53.107
Whereas, the time is changing.

00:10:53.107 --> 00:10:54.479
The youth are listening differently.

00:10:54.479 --> 00:10:56.771
They understand music better
than you think they do.

00:10:56.771 --> 00:10:59.111
And you just can't fool
the audience anymore.

00:10:59.111 --> 00:11:02.004
You have to be able to take
a shot and take a chance.

00:11:02.004 --> 00:11:04.267
You can't break anything that
you don't take a shot on.

00:11:04.267 --> 00:11:07.008
And they're out chasing the single.

00:11:07.008 --> 00:11:09.167
Records were built on an experience.

00:11:09.167 --> 00:11:11.515
Artists and superstars were
built on the experience.

00:11:11.515 --> 00:11:12.930
When you thought about Michael Jackson,

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.008
you didn't just think about Thriller

00:11:14.008 --> 00:11:16.258
or Beat It or Human Nature.

00:11:17.222 --> 00:11:20.088
You though about the
experience that came with Mike.

00:11:20.088 --> 00:11:21.745
From the performance, to the mini-movies,

00:11:21.745 --> 00:11:24.935
to the concerts, to barely
seeing him in public

00:11:24.935 --> 00:11:28.046
and you see him chasing
down that alleyway.

00:11:28.046 --> 00:11:30.459
That vision of Mike was
going to be there today

00:11:30.459 --> 00:11:31.927
and you don't know if you're ever going

00:11:31.927 --> 00:11:33.434
to be able to see him live again.

00:11:33.434 --> 00:11:34.942
We lost that.

00:11:34.942 --> 00:11:37.480
That doesn't happen anymore
because the record company

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.978
understood how to build superstars.

00:11:40.978 --> 00:11:42.900
And you can't be profitable
if you're just focused

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:46.242
on a record that you can download for free

00:11:46.242 --> 00:11:49.635
on any music related site anymore.

00:11:49.635 --> 00:11:51.031
And I think they've lost site of that.

00:11:51.031 --> 00:11:54.551
They hadn't transformed into
the digital age fast enough.

00:11:54.551 --> 00:11:56.577
Whereas, the younger youth
and the generation now

00:11:56.577 --> 00:11:58.010
understands how that works.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.393
Everyone has a MacBook
where they have Garage Band

00:12:00.393 --> 00:12:01.904
and can make their own records.

00:12:01.904 --> 00:12:04.021
And you have YouTube where
you can create your own videos

00:12:04.021 --> 00:12:05.718
and become your own superstar.

00:12:05.718 --> 00:12:06.837
So guess what?

00:12:06.837 --> 00:12:09.286
If you have that competition
and yet the artist

00:12:09.286 --> 00:12:12.764
that's making you money
don't have no extra leverage

00:12:12.764 --> 00:12:14.751
that you should be bringing to the table

00:12:14.751 --> 00:12:16.344
and dumping the money and the system

00:12:16.344 --> 00:12:18.453
that the average person don't have,

00:12:18.453 --> 00:12:20.491
you're just as popular as

00:12:20.491 --> 00:12:23.089
the most popular person on YouTube.

00:12:23.089 --> 00:12:26.217
If you just focus on one single
record and a homemade video.

00:12:26.217 --> 00:12:28.787
See, back then we used
to put a marketing plan,

00:12:28.787 --> 00:12:30.776
put money into artists and create a system

00:12:30.776 --> 00:12:32.928
that would make you
want to say I got to go

00:12:32.928 --> 00:12:34.478
pick that up, or I got to go see that.

00:12:34.478 --> 00:12:36.044
Or, what's coming next?

00:12:36.044 --> 00:12:38.363
And how will I be excited from it?

00:12:38.363 --> 00:12:39.196
They've lost that.

